          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The form, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Hacer continues Latin facere, and hice continues the history of its strong perfect fēcī. Long sound changes help explain Spanish h- and the changed vowel and consonant; this is not a direct spelling recipe. The pattern links hice historically to strong tuve, while each verb keeps its own stem."
